{"name":"Apple Pie","hex":"#caab94","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"apple pie","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pie or tart made with a filling of cooked apples.","Anything positive that is quintessentially American."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Of a bed, to make an apple-pie bed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apple_pie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Apple pie","blocks":[{"text":"An apple pie is a fruit pie in which the principal filling is apples. It generally has shortcrust pastry both above and below the filling; the upper pastry may be solid or latticed. The bottom or pastry base may be baked separately to prevent it from getting soggy. Tarte Tatin is baked with the pastry on top, but this is served the opposite way round with the fruit exposed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Apple_pie_14.jpg/330px-Apple_pie_14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_pie","wikidata":"Q1068034"},{"title":"Apple Pie (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Apple Pie is an American sitcom that aired for only two episodes on ABC on September 23 and September 30, 1978."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/87/SitcomApplePie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Pie_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q4781212"},{"title":"Apple","blocks":[{"text":"An apple is the round, edible fruit of an apple tree. Fruit trees of the orchard or domestic apple, the most widely grown in the genus, are cultivated worldwide. The tree originated in Central Asia, where its wild ancestor, Malus sieversii, is still found. Apples have been grown for thousands of years in Eurasia before they were introduced to the American continent by European colonists. Apples have cultural significance in many mythologies and religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple","wikidata":"Q89"},{"title":"Pie","blocks":[{"text":"A pie is a baked dish which is usually made of a pastry dough casing that contains a filling of various sweet or savoury ingredients. Sweet pies may be filled with fruit, nuts, fruit preserves, brown sugar, sweetened vegetables, or with thicker fillings based on eggs and dairy. Savoury pies may be filled with meat, eggs and cheese, or a mixture of meat and vegetables."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg/330px-Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pie","wikidata":"Q13360264"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Baking_a_Pie_%28Unsplash%29.jpg/500px-Baking_a_Pie_%28Unsplash%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Baking_a_Pie_%28Unsplash%29.jpg/1280px-Baking_a_Pie_%28Unsplash%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Baking_a_Pie_%28Unsplash%29.jpg/500px-Baking_a_Pie_%28Unsplash%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ingredients of an apple pie","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaking_a_Pie_(Unsplash).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Apple_cake_with_vanilla_ice_cream_2.jpg/500px-Apple_cake_with_vanilla_ice_cream_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Apple_cake_with_vanilla_ice_c